Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 18:11:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] train: port weighted-training + QAT onto v0.6.0

Port the non-redundant parts of v0.5.1 patch 0010:

  - qat.py: QuantConstraint (Hisilicon quantization-aware weight clipping),
    ported as a new module. Wired into lerobot_train.py: instantiated when
    cfg.weight_clipping is set, clip_weights() called each step after the
    optimizer update. Config knobs weight_clipping / clipping_min /
    clipping_max added to TrainPipelineConfig.
  - custom_weights: instead of v0.5.1's set_train_sample_weights + WeightSampler
    (superseded by v0.6.0's SampleWeighter framework), add a 'custom' weighter
    type to sample_weighting.py. CustomWeighter loads the dataset's
    training_weight column (written by frame_detector) and looks up per-sample
    weights via batch['index'] (v0.6.0's native frame-index channel). Enable
    with sample_weighting.type='custom'.

The v0.5.1 ada_weight/damping_coefficient knobs and WeightSampler class are
dropped: v0.6.0 ships a native SampleWeighter/SampleWeightingConfig system.
